@bank all
// W3, rec talent night (every four weeks, Sunday 19:30, the auditorium; Lucia Ferreira hosts, Maeve Volkov on
// lights). Keys for RA's show engine: talent.intro (Lucia, before each act: {name} the act's person, {thing} the act),
// talent.act.<kind> (the performer's bubble on stage: song, piano, duet, juggle, poem, trick, joke), talent.after
// (Lucia after an act), talent.open / talent.close (the start and the end), talent.crowd (a seated crowd bubble).

== talent.open
- Hello, hello! Welcome to talent night. Devices away. Hands ready.   #funny
- Good evening, Wren! Eight acts tonight, all brave, all ours. Lights please, Maeve.   #warm
== talent.intro
- Our next act needs no introduction. I'm giving one anyway. {name}!
- Please welcome a very brave person. {name}!   #funny
- Next up, {name}, with {thing}. Big hand, please.
== talent.after
- Wasn't that lovely? Give it up for {name}!   #warm
- {name}, everyone! Nobody fell off the stage. A good start.   #funny
- That's going in the newsletter. Well done, {name}.
== talent.close
- That's talent night! Thank you, all of you. Same time in four weeks. Start practising.   #warm
== talent.act.song
- This one's from home. Bear with me.   #warm
- La la... sorry, too high. Again.   #funny
== talent.act.piano
- I'll play the slow one. Shh.   #warm
== talent.act.duet
- On three. One, two... no, wait. Now.   #funny
== talent.act.juggle
- Three spanners. Four. Oh. Three again.   #funny
== talent.act.poem
- A short one. About the stars.   #warm
== talent.act.trick
- Pick a card. Not that one.   #funny
== talent.act.joke
- Why did the drive coil sulk? Coil three.   #funny
== talent.crowd
- Go on!
- Oh, that's lovely.   #warm
- Encore!   #funny
- Brave. So brave.   #funny
